# error-shaped, and the one that matters most on this command: a positional that is not a walk id is REFUSED by name. Accepted and discarded, notice would fall through to the working tree's go.mod and answer a question nobody asked, with an exit code.
$ kanonarion notice THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES
exit 20
--- error ---
execute root command: "THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES" is not a walk id: notice takes an optional walk id (a 26-character identifier, as 'kanonarion walk-list' prints), or --gomod <path> / --package <pattern> to scope from the working tree
--- stdout ---
(empty)
--- stderr ---
(empty)
